\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 2. What the colours signify\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 There are product variants; the narrative remains deliberately loose about what they mean..\
In \'93Chanta searches for the Harum Scarum clone series\'94, where Chanta discovers Grayling Corporation's packaged clones. The cartons identify the product as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 AJENT JONES\strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \strokec2 Security & Enforcement Assistant\strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \strokec2 Grayling Corporation\strokec2 \
A promotional sticker announces: \strokec2 NOW WITH NEW PINK TIE!\strokec2 \
In \'93The Moe Bogan Experience influences the Jones clones\'94, Fisher discovers a report titled: \strokec2 GRAYLING PRODUCT VARIATION \'97 POSSIBLE SIGNIFICANCE OF TIE COLOUR\strokec2 \
This is a report the Jones clones themselves have written during their investigations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 3. Continuity rules supported by the manuscript
\f0\b0\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Five colours are explicitly established: black, red, green, blue and pink.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Jones clones are manufactured by Grayling Corporation as security and enforcement assistants.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pink Tie is historically a new variation, discovered by Chanta in Hardy\'92s storage. They are not in modern distribution.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Chanta activates numerous Jones clones, including at least one of every tie colour.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tie colour is not a unique identifier for a particular Jones clone.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The existence of a systematic relationship between colour, personality, capability and intended function is deliberately kept vague.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

